 12, the record for Nash County runs 75 years, from 1951 to 2025. On the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 7 grids, September to October came in under 90% of normal in 39 of those years, more than any other pair. In 2025 that same pair ran 50% of normal, and so far in 2026 March to April sits at 46% of normal on the middle of the grids. For grid 19108, a preliminary estimate puts August to September 2026 at 42.0, and RMA&rsquo;s final index can differ.</p>"}
